I recently saw some strange behavior from a shopkeeper.  He had
fallen through a trap door that I had dug and was stuck in the rock
between rooms.  Just for kicks I dug him out, and he seemed to be
asleep.  When I attacked him (just for kicks) he fought back but
didn't pursue when I ran.  Then, and here's the really strange
part, after several minutes of exploring the level, he finally
decided to get up and run for about 15 moves.  After this he just
stopped and seemed to be asleep again.  Well, seeing that he was down
on his luck, I decided to nuke him with my wand of lightning.

Is there an explanation for his behavior?  Perhaps the program sensed my
bad disposition and couldn't cope.

Anyway, this gave me an idea:



The merchandise in the shop on the level above was mine for the taking.
No Kops appeared when I took it.  This would be an easy way to steal
provided that a shopkeeper would step on a trap door regularly.  (He was
still peaceful after falling through the trap door.)  But, when I started
another game in wizard mode to test the idea, I couldn't get a shopkeeper
to step on my trap.

Evidently, a shopkeeper will sometimes step on a trap; I have seen it
happen at least one other time too.  Is there a way to coax him onto a trap?

Happy Robbing,

Ken


